{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And they were grieved, etc., for a vile thing, etc.</b> The meaning is that there are in this deed two matters of provocation: the first is that even if he had taken her for himself as a wife in the customary manner of the world, even so it would be a disgrace for them to give their daughter to an impure man — and this is what it says afterward, <b>for he has done a vile thing in Israel, to lie with the daughter of Jacob</b>; and corresponding to this aspect it says <b>and the men were grieved</b>. The second is on account of doing the thing in such a manner — that even among the nations who are comparable in the category of lowliness, it is a reprehensible thing — and this is what it says <b>and so it shall not be done</b>, meaning even among the nations, as they said, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 80:6), that the nations had fenced themselves off from illicit relations. And corresponding to this it says <b>and it burned for them</b> — how he did a thing that even among themselves is improper:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:51.583763531Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}